Why This Market Matters
Bispecific antibodies represent an important class of engineered biologics capable of engaging two distinct targets within a single therapeutic construct. Their ability to combine immune-cell recruitment, tumor targeting, or pathway modulation is supporting the development of differentiated therapies. Continued clinical progress and expansion into additional indications are creating opportunities for pharmaceutical and biotechnology companies.

